From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: a name we do not have must not erase the one we do

sta.hostname was written and gone again 59 seconds later.

The sta upsert guards every other column that can arrive unknown:
est_mac_rate_ul/dl keep the last positive value, rcpi keeps the last real
reading. hostname was the one left plain - "hostname=excluded.hostname" -
and nothing on the agent path ever fills it, so each upsert wrote NULL over
whatever was there.

Measured 2026-09-07 on the lab mesh. The name was put into the row from the
DHCP leases; 59 s later, after one upsert:

  62:35  hostname=NULL   ipv4=172.16.20.188   last_seen 59 s ago
  17:82  hostname=iPhone ipv4=172.16.20.166   last_seen 323 s ago

The client whose row had been rewritten had lost its name; the one that had
not kept it. ipv4 survived on both - and ipv4 is not in this statement at
all. That is what points at the statement rather than at the writer.

It matters more than a cosmetic column. The only source of a client's name
is /tmp/dhcp.leases, which is RAM: after a controller restart a name comes
back only when that client happens to renew its lease, measured at up to 12
hours. Persisting it is the entire purpose of the column, and this line was
undoing it every minute.

Same shape as rcpi, est_thput and conn_time: a value that was never measured
must not outrank one that was.

Verify: write a hostname into sta, wait for the client's next upsert, and
the name must still be there.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/db/mapc_sync.c
+++ b/src/db/mapc_sync.c
@@ -620,7 +620,25 @@
 		"pkts_tx=excluded.pkts_tx, pkts_rx=excluded.pkts_rx, "
 		"bytes_tx=excluded.bytes_tx, bytes_rx=excluded.bytes_rx, "
 		"errors_tx=excluded.errors_tx, errors_rx=excluded.errors_rx, "
-		"retrans_count=excluded.retrans_count, hostname=excluded.hostname, "
+		"retrans_count=excluded.retrans_count, "
+		/* A name we do not have must not erase the name we do.
+		 *
+		 * Every other column that can arrive unknown is already guarded
+		 * two lines up - est_mac_rate keeps the last positive value, rcpi
+		 * keeps the last real reading. hostname was the one left plain,
+		 * and nothing on the agent path fills it, so each upsert wrote
+		 * NULL over whatever was there.
+		 *
+		 * Measured 2026-09-07: the name was written into the row and was
+		 * gone 59 s later, at the next upsert, while ipv4 - which is not
+		 * in this statement at all - survived. That is the tell.
+		 *
+		 * It matters because the only source of a client's name is
+		 * /tmp/dhcp.leases, which is RAM: after a controller restart the
+		 * name comes back only when the client happens to renew, measured
+		 * at up to 12 h. The column exists precisely so that does not
+		 * have to be waited for. */
+		"hostname=COALESCE(NULLIF(excluded.hostname,''), sta.hostname), "
 		"last_seen=excluded.last_seen, "
 		"first_seen=COALESCE(sta.first_seen, excluded.first_seen)";
 	struct wifi_sta_element *d = s->de_sta;
